# Trivy IaC findings accepted as by-design or platform-limited for this app.
# Each entry documents WHY it's not fixed in code. Re-review if the underlying
# design assumption changes (e.g. sit gets an ACM cert, WAF budget approved).

# ALB is intentionally internet-facing: it's the public entry point for a
# customer-facing shopping cart web app.
AWS-0053

# HttpListener exists unconditionally so `sit` can run without an ACM cert
# (see alb.yaml CertificateArn parameter). When a cert is supplied, HTTP
# redirects to HTTPS; uat/prd are expected to always supply a cert.
AWS-0054

# ConnectionStrings__DbSecretArn carries a Secrets Manager ARN, not a secret
# value, so the ECS task can fetch/rotate it via SDK. Trivy's check flags the
# variable NAME (contains "Secret") regardless of content sensitivity.
AWS-0036

# CloudFront's MinimumProtocolVersion cannot be set together with
# CloudFrontDefaultCertificate (AWS restriction) - it only applies once a
# custom domain + ACM cert is supplied, where it's already TLSv1.2_2021.
AWS-0013

# Adding a WAFv2 WebACL (CLOUDFRONT scope) requires deploying in us-east-1
# and picking managed rule groups/rate limits - a deliberate follow-up, not
# a drop-in fix, since it's a new billable resource.
AWS-0011
